From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] syscall_wrappers: use the kernel struct open_how when the
 system has openat2

configure now detects openat2(2) and defines HAVE_OPENAT2, so lxc's own
static inline wrapper is compiled out and the system prototype - which takes
struct open_how * - is what the call sites see. They still pass lxc's private
struct lxc_open_how *, which GCC 15 rejects outright:

  file_utils.c:661:33: error: passing argument 3 of 'openat2' from
  incompatible pointer type [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]

The two structs are byte-identical (three __u64: flags, mode, resolve), so
alias lxc_open_how to the kernel's open_how when it is available and keep the
private definition only for the fallback path. This leaves all eight call
sites untouched.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/lxc/syscall_wrappers.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lxc/syscall_wrappers.h b/src/lxc/syscall_wrappers.h
index dbfa018..564a679 100644
--- a/src/lxc/syscall_wrappers.h
+++ b/src/lxc/syscall_wrappers.h
@@ -247,11 +247,21 @@ static inline int mount_setattr_lxc(int dfd, const char *path, unsigned int flag
  * @mode: O_CREAT/O_TMPFILE file mode.
  * @resolve: RESOLVE_* flags.
  */
+#if HAVE_OPENAT2
+/*
+ * The system provides openat2(2), and with it the kernel's own struct
+ * open_how. Alias to it so the call sites below match the real prototype
+ * rather than a private struct of identical layout.
+ */
+#include <linux/openat2.h>
+#define lxc_open_how open_how
+#else
 struct lxc_open_how {
 	__u64 flags;
 	__u64 mode;
 	__u64 resolve;
 };
+#endif
 
 /* how->resolve flags for openat2(2). */
 #ifndef RESOLVE_NO_XDEV
